\uline{Theorem 2} The functor $K-\Pi_K/\Pi_{\mathbb Q}$ from finitely generated extensions of $\mathbb Q$ to profinite groupoids over $\Pi_{\mathbb Q}$ is \uline{faithful}.

\margin{In fact, this theorem is not special to $\mathbb Q$ --- it would work over any base field of characteristic $0$. \unsure{The|for the} proof clearly shows that it is in fact a statement of a geometric non-arithmetic nature (\unsure{I state|the statement} to \unsure{make} the proof easy \unsure{and|an} \unsure{arithmetic|intuitively} \unsure{pure|short}).}

If two homomorphisms $K\overset{f,g}{\rightrightarrows}K'$ define isomorphic homomorphisms of groupoids \inserted{over $\Pi_{\mathbb Q}$}
\diagram{\begin{tikzcd}[ampersand replacement=\&]
\Pi_{K'} \arrow[r,shift left,"f^*"] \arrow[r,shift right,"g^*"'] \arrow[dr,no head,"p'"'] \& \Pi_K \arrow[d,"p"]\\
\& \Pi_{\mathbb Q}
\end{tikzcd}}
(that is, $\exists$ isomorphism of functors $\alpha:f^*\simeq g^*$, such that $\forall\bar\eta'\in\operatorname{Ob}\Pi_{K'}$, the \deleted{isomorphism}\inserted{square}
\deleted{corresponding}
\diagram{\begin{tikzcd}[ampersand replacement=\&]
pf^*(\bar\eta') \arrow[r,phantom,"{\overset{p(\alpha)}{\simeq}}" description] \arrow[d,"\wr"'] \& pg^*(\unsure{\eta|\eta'}) \arrow[d,no head,"\wr"]\\
p'(\bar\eta') \arrow[r,phantom,"\simeq" description] \& p'(\bar\eta')
\end{tikzcd}}
\unsure{is|is} commutative) then $f=g$.

The hypothesis on $f,g$ also means, in terms of a chosen algebraic closure $\bar K'$ \deleted{\unsure{which|which one} \unsure{can}}\inserted{giving via $f,g$ two algebraic closures of $\unsure{K_\varepsilon|\bar K}$, $\unsure{K|\widetilde K}$ of $K$} of $K'$, that \deleted{the two homomorphisms of extensions}\inserted{one can find an isomorphism between these (thus allowing one to identify $E_{\bar K/K}$ and $E_{\widetilde K/K}$), in such a way that the two homomorphisms}
\deleted{\unsure{say}}
\margin{inducing ``the identity'' on the algebraic closures \deleted{\unsure{and|of}} $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $\mathbb Q$ in $\bar K$ and $\widetilde K$, identified with the one in $\bar K'$.}
\[
f^*,g^*:E_{\bar K'/K'}\rightrightarrows E_{\bar K/K}
\]
are equal, \deleted{It \unsure{(This)|It is} \unsure{is a matter} \unsure{in} \unsure{therefore} \unsure{more} \unsure{conclusion}}
\unsure{Or else} in terms of a fixed algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, of $\mathbb Q$, by saying that the two homomorphisms $f^*,g^*:\pi_{K'}\rightrightarrows\pi_K$ of outer profinite groups (with operators $\Gamma_{\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q}$) are equal.
\margin{One must reduce to the case $k=k'$ --- this is immediate by \deleted{\unsure{making the base change}}\inserted{\unsure{taking}} finite extension of $\mathbb Q$.}
